---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { gccRegion } from '../../regions/gcc';

const gateway = (slug: string) => gccRegion.ports.find((p) => p.country === slug);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="China to GCC country guides"
  description="China to Saudi Arabia, the UAE, Qatar, Kuwait, Oman and Bahrain: customs duty, VAT, certification, gateway ports and route context for each market."
>
  <h1>China to GCC country guides</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Six markets share one sourcing origin, but not one import regime. Duty rates, VAT, certification
    requirements and the port that makes sense all differ. Each country guide answers the same four
    questions in the same order so they can be read side by side.
  </p>

  <figure class="drawing-figure">
    <img src="/images/map-gcc-ports.png" alt="GCC port system map: the six markets and their gateways, with seaports and Riyadh dry port." width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    <figcaption>Drawing 07 — Where the six markets sit and which gateways serve them. Base map Natural Earth 1:10m; not for navigation.</figcaption>
  </figure>

<h2>The six markets at a glance</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Market</th><th>Currency</th><th>Indirect tax</th><th>Gateway</th><th>Guide</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {gccRegion.countries.map((c) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{c.name}</td>
            <td>{c.currency}</td>
            <td>{c.vat === 0 ? 'No VAT' : `${Math.round(c.vat * 100)}% VAT`}</td>
            <td>{gateway(c.slug)?.name ?? '—'}</td>
            <td><a href={`/countries/${c.slug}/`}>Open guide</a></td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>What each guide covers</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>The customs position: duty basis, valuation, and the charges that appear after arrival.</li>
    <li>Certification: which scheme applies, who issues it, and what happens when it is missing.</li>
    <li>The gateway: which port or airports serve the market, and the inland leg behind them.</li>
    <li>Route context: transit ranges by mode, and the seasonal or regulatory events that move them.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Why the differences matter</h2>
  <p>
    A landed-cost model built on one Gulf country will misprice the next. Saudi Arabia applies 15% VAT
    and requires SABER conformity for most regulated goods; the UAE applies 5% and a different
    conformity regime; Qatar and Kuwait currently apply no VAT but have their own documentation and
    inspection practice. A quote that treats "GCC" as a single destination is a quote that has not
    been checked against the destination's rules.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where a country page and a guide disagree, the country page carries the customs detail and the
    guide carries the mode economics; both name their sources. The
    <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> explains how those sources are chosen.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
